1
00:00:04,049 --> 00:00:04,895
Two teams.

2
00:00:04,945 --> 00:00:06,286
Forty-one neighborhoods.

3
00:00:06,336 --> 00:00:07,177
One clock.

4
00:00:07,227 --> 00:00:08,964
This is Clipper Conquest.

5
00:00:09,814 --> 00:00:18,010
Clipper Conquest is played by two teams, the red team and the blue team, that race to conquer as many San Francisco neighborhoods as possible.

6
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:22,189
Whichever team has more neighborhoods when the clock hits zero is the winner.

7
00:00:24,231 --> 00:00:28,018
Every one of the city's 41 neighborhoods has three unique challenges.

8
00:00:28,068 --> 00:00:33,298
For example, one challenge might ask you to get three antique arcade machines running at the same time.

9
00:00:33,348 --> 00:00:38,513
Another might ask two teammates to count the sea lions at Pier 39 and agree on the number.

10
00:00:38,563 --> 00:00:42,234
Whichever team has completed more of a neighborhood's challenges holds it.

11
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:47,973
You get around on Muni, and only Muni: buses, Metro, streetcars and cable cars.

12
00:00:48,023 --> 00:00:51,059
No BART, no Caltrain, no cars and no bikes.

13
00:00:51,109 --> 00:00:53,144
And no running unless a challenge says to.

14
00:00:53,194 --> 00:00:54,767
You can only speedwalk.

15
00:00:55,616 --> 00:00:57,563
When you finish a challenge, take a photo.

16
00:00:57,612 --> 00:00:59,401
Every completion needs one.

17
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,155
Then upload it in the app and tap Complete.

18
00:01:03,204 --> 00:01:05,735
The moment you log it is the moment it counts.

19
00:01:06,585 --> 00:01:08,684
Here's how that plays out in North Beach.

20
00:01:09,534 --> 00:01:11,028
The blue team completes one.

21
00:01:11,078 --> 00:01:13,001
North Beach is the blue team's.

22
00:01:13,852 --> 00:01:14,775
But be careful.

23
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:18,954
The other team can steal a neighborhood by completing more of its challenges than you.

24
00:01:19,004 --> 00:01:20,566
The red team completes one.

25
00:01:20,615 --> 00:01:24,885
Now it's one each, but the blue team got there first, so North Beach stays blue.

26
00:01:25,736 --> 00:01:26,624
And then another.

27
00:01:26,674 --> 00:01:27,649
Two beats one.

28
00:01:27,698 --> 00:01:29,681
The red team steals North Beach.

29
00:01:30,531 --> 00:01:32,304
The blue team answers with a second.

30
00:01:32,353 --> 00:01:33,400
Now it's two each.

31
00:01:33,450 --> 00:01:34,753
So who holds it?

32
00:01:35,603 --> 00:01:38,016
Ties go to whichever team reached that count first.

33
00:01:38,066 --> 00:01:40,864
The red team logged its second at 11:58.

34
00:01:40,914 --> 00:01:43,441
The blue team logged its second at 12:30.

35
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:45,528
So the red team keeps North Beach.

36
00:01:46,379 --> 00:01:48,759
Complete all three and the neighborhood is locked.

37
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:50,216
No one can steal it.

38
00:01:54,579 --> 00:01:55,656
So there's a choice.

39
00:01:55,706 --> 00:01:58,909
One challenge grabs a neighborhood fast, but it can be stolen.

40
00:01:58,959 --> 00:02:00,859
All three lock it, but that takes time.

41
00:02:00,909 --> 00:02:05,777
Here, the red team zips around grabbing neighborhoods, while the blue team locks down a few.

42
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:10,061
Whichever team has more neighborhoods when the clock hits zero wins.

43
00:02:10,111 --> 00:02:12,776
Every rule and every challenge is in the guide.

